  "readings": [
    {
      "id": "U11L-READ-1",
      "title": "My Cousin's War Game",
      "text": "My cousin plays a war game every night. In the game, players join a military team, move their troops, and capture the enemy's base. Each battle takes about ten minutes. Every player can pick a weapon, but the game is fair: everyone starts with the same money. Last week my cousin created his own map. He is very creative, and other players said his map was worth trying. Some of them said the old maps were worse. His room is always in a mess when he plays, so his mother asks him to put away his clothes and cups first. She cannot put up with the noise, either. My cousin has faith in his own plan: he wants to study computer science and create games for a living."
    }
  ],
